<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry V, Count Palatine of the Rhine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1173–<a href="/years/1227">1227</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Henry the Elder of Brunswick</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, became count palatine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in 1195 through his marriage to Agnes, heiress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-count-palatine-of-the-rhine">Conrad of Hohenstaufen</a>. A brother of Emperor Otto IV, he took part in the Welf struggle for the German throne. The palatinate was granted to the Wittelsbach Louis I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1214, and Henry spent his last years on his Brunswick lands, dying in 1227.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-v-count-palatine-of-the-rhine.jpg" alt="Henry V, Count Palatine of the Rhine" width="320" height="516" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wgt_Stifterb%C3%BCchlein_36r.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
